  <name>Lambdock</name>
  <summary>Customizable Wayland desktop dock</summary>

  <developer id="org.jointhefreeworld">
    <name>Josep Bigorra</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Lambdock is a Wayland-native desktop dock for GNU/Linux, in the spirit of
      Cairo-Dock, Plank and the macOS Dock. It is built with GTK4 and
      gtk4-layer-shell, and can be themed, extended and reconfigured live with
      GNU Guile Scheme.
    </p>
    <p>Features include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Dynamic window tracking via the Wayland foreign-toplevel protocol</li>
      <li>Multi-monitor support and multiple dock instances</li>
      <li>Auto-hide with fluid slide-out animations</li>
      <li>GTK CSS themes and configurable application launchers</li>
      <li>Dynamic widgets for CPU, RAM, temperature and more</li>
      <li>An embedded Guile runtime with hot-reloading and an optional REPL</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

